The first two images are close-ups and the last two show the same place with more surroundings. The red contour marks the same region in all of them. First find the object inside the contour at the same position in both dates, and compare its outline, roof structure and neighbouring fixed objects. Is there evidence that a building was newly constructed, demolished, or replaced by a different building? If both dates show the same building and only its color, shadow, occlusion or visibility differs, answer no. Do not read poor visibility as demolition. The reason must name the evidence of correspondence or change. Reply with JSON only: {"change": "yes" or "no", "type": one of ["new_building", "demolished", "rebuilt", "shadow", "seasonal_or_color", "misregistration", "vehicle_or_temporary", "non_building_change", "no_change"], "reason": one short sentence}
The yellow mark 1 identifies the candidate inside the existing red contour in all four views; it is an annotation, not image evidence.
Use the same change definition above. Before the final change decision, describe the object at T1 and T2, whether they are the same persisting object, and any appearance-only explanation. Return JSON with t1_state, t2_state, same_object, appearance_only, change, type, reason. The change field must still be yes or no, using the same decision rule as above.
